  2601	## D203 · 2026-10-28 · A statement day is an ISO day or unknown; the writer never fills it with the publication day
  2602	
  2603	- Found while reading D202's regression week: the extraction answer's `original_day` is a free string (54 of the three-month run's 2,369 raw pieces carry a month, a range or text; 1,445 are empty) and the writer filled every empty day with the item's publication day, against D245's rule that an unknown stays unknown. A range read as "older than" the denial it answered dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report from the week ledger.
  2604	- Decided, at the owners: `extraction.statement_day` keeps an ISO day and blanks anything else when the answer is sifted (the quote and `event_time` keep the period as written); `writing._store_piece` stores the stated day or '' and the revision path stores the stated day too (the ordering day `new_day` orders the revision only). Readers print the blank; matching's `said_day` still falls back to the publication day for ordering, never for storage. Tests: `test_a_statement_day_is_an_iso_day_or_unknown…` (red on the old sift), `test_an_unknown_statement_day_is_stored_unknown…` (red on the old writer); suite 211; preflight B/C/D unchanged.
  2605	- The judge's revision note is labelled as what it is: "Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of eX; both are in force" (D202's census: 19 of 37 recorded revisions carry a wrong label).
  2761	## D220 · 2026-10-29 · Judge necessary meaning by its investment consequence
  2762	
  2763	- Alex: “你来修正对齐，你是 hedge fund analyst 你来做好标准”. This authorizes the analyst judgement needed to finish the standard without another user adjudication round. V4 made some incidental source details mandatory and then scored their absence as lost meaning. The [full 16-item audit](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/gold-v5-2026-10-29/change-audit.md) finds three instances: G04's intermediary BofA, G09's ordinary conference-call venue, and G10's paid subscription brand name. All values, original sources and user case decisions remain unchanged. Independent review also found G14 omitted the target-price horizon from required meaning; preserve FY2028-end explicitly, since the earnings period alone does not specify the investment horizon. The six retained historical valuation answers already preserve it.
  2764	- V5's rule: a required meaning component must affect the business interpretation, valuation calculation, risk, scope of applicability, or evidentiary nature. Original claimant and estimate-versus-measurement remain necessary. A relay outlet or ordinary speaking venue need not be repeated in the summary when omission does not change authority, legal effect or chronology. Fabricated source details still count as record errors. Readable [standard](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/gold-v5-2026-10-29/README.md) and [case list](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/gold-v5-2026-10-29/reference.md).
  2765	- The same standard governs extraction acceptance: preserve linked meaning and conditions, including useful forecasts, conditional valuation arguments and counterevidence. A standalone price target does not substitute for its valuation argument. The user's excluded Singapore case must not be required by a positive prompt example. Unknown original dates cannot be invented from publication dates; candidate fiscal conventions cannot rewrite an ambiguous source period. These are acceptance requirements, not a claim that the old runtime prompt now satisfies them.
  2766	- Preserve V4 and its read results. Reassess the same 48 saved answers with V5; the source-venue-only penalty on Luna/revenue-clean-3/G09 is removed, while its time-field problem remains. This changes evaluation, not product behaviour or model capability. No new product call, default promotion or full-pipeline run is part of this standards correction.
  2874	## D237 · 2026-10-29 · The extraction prompt is a general hedge-fund brain: scrub it, then measure the whole bench
  2875	
  2876	- Alex: "You can use examples from different domains to teach the agent in the prompt to give it examples, but you can't directly hard code it. I think it's a thing that you need to look at for the prompt. The prompt is not purpose-built for NVIDIA extraction only. You're not doing this the right way. It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain. I keep on telling you this, and you keep on cherry picking the results just to meet the metrics or the benchmarks. This is not okay. You need to do a general fixed scrub and then give me the benchmark numbers on what its current performance on our test bench."
  2877	- Decided: the one-sentence arms of D232/D235/D236 were written against the bench pages' failures and checked on those pages; they are evidence of mechanisms, not the method. The extraction request is scrubbed as a whole: every rule and example must read the same for any covered company and sector; examples teach from varied domains and none comes from the test articles or names the covered company; the signed standard (D229, D231–D236) is the only source of rules. The scrubbed request is then measured once on the whole bench (the week's 98 articles and the 20-article holdout, three draws, reference v2, labelled in full like the baseline), and every number is reported against the role-v22 baseline, regressions first.
  2924	## D243 · 2026-10-29 · The extraction standard is signed: proposal 5 stricter, the other eleven at their leans; lean cautious, catch the increment
  2925	
  2926	- Alex, on the twelve proposals of `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`: "5. 这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳"; "然后你基本上也理解了这个核心，不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过"; "其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off, 你重新整合这个prd 和agentmd and readme 我们要开始重新跑了".
  2927	- Decided: proposals 1–4 and 6–12 as their leans. Proposal 5 as Alex wrote it: a typical claim or background statement is common knowledge, what an analyst following the company knew before reading the item (who leads, who competes, demand is strong, supply is tight, a known state retold), and is not kept unless it carries a number and a specific narrative. A statement that is not common knowledge (a new report's judgement, a new market data point, the detail of something that just happened) is new information and is judged by the keep rule like any statement. The general direction, in his words, governs extraction as a whole: lean cautious, the page is mostly noise, and new information that adds to an answer is not missed.
  2928	- The page becomes version 3 and replaces the signed first version (D229) as the one ruler for extraction; AGENTS.md §8 points to it. The golden set is fixed under these decisions by `golden-v3/finalize.py` into `golden-v3-signed.json` (sha256 78844bc329fc85000e18ddcab9ea59feb57abe6407cf11bbead4ba8fe4c3c0d3): 348 entries to keep or optionally keep (week 80 core, 152 supporting, 63 optional; holdout 6, 29, 18), 738 sentences not kept and 24 more now optional, every span found verbatim in its article. 39 changes, each with its reason: 24 common-knowledge claims without a number and a specific narrative and one characterising quote left the kept list; 19 entries kept and rejected at once (the blind-check additions had not been compared with the drafters' rejected sentences) were settled. A read-only review of the first integration found the claim rule applied to every named claim rather than to typical ones, and a distant forecast written as always supporting; both were corrected to Alex's words and the leans, and nine specific new statements returned to the gold. The 20 holdout articles were seen in the earlier prompt loop, so a fresh held-out set is written before the first prompt arm.
